\[\theta (a) = 1 + (\lambda_1^2 - 2 \lambda_1 + 1) = \lambda_1^2.\]If $a = \lambda_2,$ then $\theta (a) = 1 + (a - 1)^2 \approx 0.8458,$ which implies that
\[\theta^3 (a) = \lambda_1,\]so
